    <item>
      <headword id="d0e761">sitig</headword>
      <description>a layer of dung manure and seaweed alternately put together during late winter and early spring; good for all crops.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e770">feamainn dubh</headword>
      <description>cut when tide is out. High tide bringing the cut seaweed on to foreshore gathered and spread on machair soil suitable for potatoes.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e779">feamainn dearg</headword>
      <description>brought on to shore by the incoming tide; also suitable for potatoes as is also for oats and barley.</description>
    </item>
